🔄 Data Pipeline

The pipeline follows an ETL/ELT architecture:

Extract — ingestion of raw sales data from external sources.
Load — storage of raw data in the Bronze layer.
Transform — cleaning, normalization and transformation using Python and Pandas.
Data Quality — validation of null values, duplicates, data types and business rules.
Load — processed data is stored in analytical structures.
Analytics — SQL queries and Power BI dashboards are used for analysis.
🗂️ Data Architecture

The project uses a layered architecture:

Bronze

Raw data stored without business transformations.

Silver

Cleaned and standardized datasets.

Gold

Business-ready analytical tables following dimensional modeling principles.

dim_customer
dim_product
dim_date
fact_sales
⚙️ Orchestration

Apache Airflow is responsible for scheduling and orchestrating the pipeline.

Example DAG:

Extract
   ↓
Validate Raw Data
   ↓
Transform
   ↓
Load
   ↓
Data Quality
   ↓
Analytics

The pipeline includes task dependencies, retries and execution logs.

🧪 Data Quality

The pipeline validates:

Required fields
Duplicate records
Invalid dates
Negative prices
Invalid quantities
Referential integrity
Data types

Invalid datasets are prevented from being loaded into the analytical layer.

🐳 Running Locally

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-user/dataflow-analytics-pipeline.git

cd dataflow-analytics-pipeline

Start the development environment:

docker compose up -d

The project can then be executed through the Airflow environment.

